From e372e6e6f075f519b0cb3f71072596b4d815a0ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:34:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] close the 768-1023px navigation hole and make the map chrome
 measurable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three defects, all found by measurement rather than by reading:

1. No navigation at all from 768px to 1023px. useMobile.tsx moved
   MOBILE_BREAKPOINT from 768 to 1024 in an earlier stage; the header's
   trigger kept `md:hidden`. In that band the sidebar had not mounted and
   the trigger was already hidden — iPad Pro 11 portrait (834), iPad Air
   portrait (820) and any split-screen window could not navigate. Probed
   at 375/700/767/768/900/1024: burgerVisible went false at 768 and the
   sidebar did not appear until 1024.

2. Map chrome overlapped itself at every viewport. Projects.tsx rendered
   an "Interaktive Projektkarte" card `absolute bottom-6 left-6` OUTSIDE
   the map, so it anchored to the page and landed on the map's legend:
   36,252px² of overlap from 375px to 1440px, hiding 41% of it. It also
   claimed to show "alle N gefilterten Projekte" while the map itself
   reports how many have no station and no BM. Deleted, not moved — the
   Netz-Explorer card already carries the honest counts.

   Overlays covered 58.9% of a 289x596 map on an iPhone SE. Now 34.3%
   closed, 0px² mutual overlap, 0 spill, at six device profiles in both
   legend states.

3. Two routes overflowed 375px: Dashboard 406/375 (a fixed w-64 select
   beside a title in a 327px box) and PSV-ITK 390/375 ("Projektvorstel-
   lungen" at text-4xl is one unbreakable word). Page titles were also
   two different sizes across five pages and none responsive; they now
   share a `page-title` utility.

Also:
- Legend is a disclosure, closed below 640px, two columns on a phone,
  keyboard operable, initial state read during useState rather than in
  an effect so there is no open-then-close jump.
- Map control placement switches on POINTER, not width: touch hides
  Leaflet's zoom (pinch is native) and takes the bottom-right corner a
  thumb can reach; mouse keeps zoom bottom-right and the cluster top-right.
- Approximate (region-centroid) markers are hollow rings, not dashed
  circles — a 2px dash on a 26px circle rasterises into a cog.
- .db-dot unscoped from .db-dot-marker so legend swatches are round.
- 7,795 table controls measured 32px on touch. The box stays 32px for
  density; a transparent ::after gives each a 44px hit area, which fits
  inside the measured 57px row pitch with 6.5px to spare. Verified by
  tapping 18px above a cell's visual centre and getting the editor.
- check-responsive.mjs could not launch in a container at all (no
  --no-sandbox). Fixed, given the 1024 boundary, seven viewports
  including 820 and 834, and a breakpoint-agnostic "navigation is
  reachable" assertion. 61 assertions, all passing.
- New scripts/check-map-chrome.mjs walks Leaflet's own controls as well
  as the React overlays — the blind spot that let the collision through.
- Both layout gates now run in CI beside pnpm e2e.

Gates: 0 type errors · 129 passed / 6 skipped · 80 lint warnings
(unchanged) · build clean · e2e 22/22 · responsive 61/61 · map chrome
6/6 profiles.
